WEBVTT

00:06.030 --> 00:10.630
usu murasaki hirogaru

00:06.030 --> 00:10.630
The faint purple spreads across the sky

00:10.630 --> 00:18.610
orenji iro ni kawaru mado no soto

00:10.630 --> 00:18.610
The color changes to orange outside the window

00:18.610 --> 00:22.660
yoru wa mou bai bai

00:18.610 --> 00:22.660
The night's already "bye-bye"

00:23.210 --> 00:28.900
tada kirei na mono wo kirei to

00:23.210 --> 00:28.900
I just want to be someone who

00:28.900 --> 00:33.460
ieru atashi de itai

00:28.900 --> 00:33.460
calls beautiful things beautiful

00:33.460 --> 00:39.800
ima wa dokidoki shitai no

00:33.460 --> 00:39.800
I want to get excited for it!

00:40.330 --> 00:44.860
fumidashichae tomaranai

00:40.330 --> 00:44.860
So I step out, unstoppable

00:44.860 --> 00:49.450
zenbu te ni hairi sou de

00:44.860 --> 00:49.450
And take everything into my own hands

00:49.940 --> 00:54.050
sono saki de aitai

00:49.940 --> 00:54.050
Beyond there, I want to meet

00:54.050 --> 01:00.040
mita koto no nai atashi

00:54.050 --> 01:00.040
the new self that I've never seen

01:00.510 --> 01:05.160
sayonara daisuki na machi

01:00.510 --> 01:05.160
Farewell, my beloved town

01:05.160 --> 01:09.710
atashi mo ganbatte miru yo

01:05.160 --> 01:09.710
I'll try to do my best

01:09.710 --> 01:17.270
kono sora no tsuzuku basho de

01:09.710 --> 01:17.270
somewhere under the same sky

01:22.390 --> 01:26.810
Situation 12

01:22.390 --> 01:26.810
Who's the Library for?

01:30.310 --> 01:32.900
Regarding Dojo Atsushi,

01:32.900 --> 01:36.010
he did not sustain any external injuries.

01:36.010 --> 01:37.400
No broken bones,

01:37.400 --> 01:42.830
but he is showing signs of agnosia and dysfunction of the executive systems.

01:43.530 --> 01:44.830
Agnosia?

01:45.530 --> 01:48.500
He cannot recognize our faces or understand the words we're saying,

01:49.000 --> 01:52.020
and he can't do anything on his own, either.

01:52.020 --> 02:00.690
His brain isn't damaged, so I believe that these are temporary symptoms that stem from the shock of his injury.

02:02.960 --> 02:04.100
Instructor!

02:05.070 --> 02:06.890
It's me!

02:06.890 --> 02:08.260
Instructor!

02:18.890 --> 02:20.910
Instructor Dojo!

02:22.760 --> 02:23.850
How's Dojo?

02:25.200 --> 02:31.170
Captain Genda miraculously survived, but he hasn't regained consciousness.

02:31.890 --> 02:34.460
If they stay in their current states...

02:34.460 --> 02:35.760
Tezuka,

02:36.620 --> 02:38.140
don't worry.

02:38.140 --> 02:41.560
You know they're both the reckless type.

02:41.560 --> 02:46.040
They went too far this time, so it's just taking them longer to recover than usual.

02:46.040 --> 02:47.490
They'll be fine in no time.

02:50.900 --> 02:57.490
Opposition to the Library Force is increasing because there were casualties among the Media Cleansing Force during this conflict.

02:57.490 --> 03:02.700
We asked some people for their opinions on this incident.

03:02.700 --> 03:05.720
Censorship is a rule set by the government.

03:05.720 --> 03:08.420
It's the Library Force's fault for not following their rules.

03:08.420 --> 03:14.630
We could've avoided this wretched situation if only the Library Force hadn't resisted the censorship.

03:14.630 --> 03:17.580
What're they saying?

03:17.580 --> 03:22.020
This station has always been biased towards the Media Cleansing Committee.

03:22.020 --> 03:23.550
Still!

03:23.550 --> 03:27.110
But the Library Force suffered injuries as well.

03:27.110 --> 03:32.140
They acted against the law, so it's their own fault.

03:32.140 --> 03:34.720
Our own fault?

03:34.720 --> 03:35.980
Why...

03:35.980 --> 03:38.460
They have no idea about anything!

03:40.900 --> 03:45.660
Please let me know immediately if either of them shows signs of recovery.

03:45.660 --> 03:46.790
Yes, Sir.

03:48.200 --> 03:49.700
Shibasaki.

03:49.700 --> 03:51.230
Yes.

03:51.230 --> 03:52.870
I have high hopes for you.

03:52.870 --> 03:54.140
Yes?

03:54.140 --> 04:01.420
I heard a rumor that you want to become the first female commander in the history of the Library Force.

04:02.260 --> 04:04.430
Well, that's...

04:05.410 --> 04:09.390
Please don't give up on that ambition.

04:10.290 --> 04:12.200
Commander Inamine...

04:20.480 --> 04:23.740
The Library Force has to follow the censorships set by the government!

04:23.740 --> 04:24.950
Disband immediately!

04:24.950 --> 04:27.740
Don't resist censorship!

05:03.980 --> 05:06.280
What are you doing?

05:07.500 --> 05:10.160
Trying to master gun kata?

05:10.160 --> 05:16.250
Is this your way of wishing Instructor Dojo well?

05:17.500 --> 05:19.470
It's not that.

05:19.470 --> 05:23.340
He'll recover soon, even if I don't do anything.

05:23.340 --> 05:29.970
But if I don't change at all before he recovers, I couldn't possibly face him.

05:30.630 --> 05:33.020
You're such a girl.

05:35.680 --> 05:37.110
Kasahara!

05:39.020 --> 05:43.400
You're going to visit Dojo after work as usual, right?

05:43.400 --> 05:44.320
Then...

05:44.320 --> 05:46.090
What's this?

05:46.090 --> 05:48.140
Dojo's favorite books.

05:48.140 --> 05:51.000
Would you read these to him?

05:51.000 --> 05:53.120
Instructor Dojo's?

05:53.120 --> 05:56.410
I heard they influenced him a lot when he read them in his teens.

05:56.890 --> 06:01.630
I tried to think whether there's anything I could do for him.

06:02.450 --> 06:04.810
Instructor Komaki...

06:04.810 --> 06:06.370
Thank you.

06:06.370 --> 06:11.790
Oh, two of those are subject to censorship, so be careful with the Cleansing Committee.

06:11.790 --> 06:12.600
Okay.

06:16.490 --> 06:22.480
"Because of a hereditary recklessness, I have always been playing a losing game since my childhood."

06:29.410 --> 06:34.240
"During my grammar school days, I was once laid up for about a week by..."

06:45.390 --> 06:49.260
Don't panic so easily, idiots!

06:53.380 --> 06:55.510
Genda!

06:55.510 --> 06:56.440
Where are we?

06:57.370 --> 06:59.910
In a hospital, of course.

06:59.910 --> 07:02.980
You were shot 32 times all over your body,

07:02.980 --> 07:05.900
and you went through a major operation that lasted 13 hours!

07:08.220 --> 07:09.370
The artwork?

07:09.370 --> 07:11.030
It's safe.

07:11.030 --> 07:14.200
The event ended safely as well.

07:14.200 --> 07:16.080
I see.

07:19.280 --> 07:21.400
Please.

07:21.400 --> 07:23.960
I don't like seeing you cry.

07:25.270 --> 07:28.470
Have a good look, as your punishment for being so reckless.

07:30.120 --> 07:35.990
Genda Ryusuke, Library Supervisor Third Class, is to be promoted to Library Supervisor First Class.

07:35.990 --> 07:39.890
Kanto Library Force Commander, Inamine Kazuichi.

07:40.860 --> 07:43.110
A two-grade promotion?

07:43.110 --> 07:45.540
I didn't die!

07:45.540 --> 07:46.800
No!

07:46.800 --> 07:48.320
We know.

07:48.320 --> 07:51.260
Nobody thinks you're dead.

07:51.260 --> 07:54.780
He wanted to give this to you when you were conscious again.

07:55.640 --> 07:57.010
The Commander did?

07:58.820 --> 08:00.960
It must be his last present.

08:00.960 --> 08:03.390
He said he'll entrust the group to you.

08:03.390 --> 08:04.990
What?

08:04.990 --> 08:08.790
During the conflict at the exhibit, there were casualties from the Cleansing Force,

08:08.790 --> 08:12.340
and the public is demanding action from the Library.

08:12.340 --> 08:14.610
And is he...

08:15.560 --> 08:18.010
What do you mean?!

08:18.010 --> 08:20.190
It's just as I explained.

08:20.980 --> 08:25.260
But Commander Inamine is taking responsibility by resigning?!

08:25.260 --> 08:26.860
Did the Governmentalists plan this?!

08:26.860 --> 08:29.080
Watch what you say!

08:29.080 --> 08:34.200
Commander Admiral Hikoe, a Governmentalist, said that he will take the blame himself.

08:34.690 --> 08:37.800
This resignation is done solely based on the Commander's will.

08:44.010 --> 08:49.250
You took care of me when we were abducted, too.

08:49.250 --> 08:51.130
It's not a problem at all.

08:55.580 --> 08:57.140
Salute!

09:00.310 --> 09:02.790
We will now receive words from Commander Inamine.

09:02.790 --> 09:03.940
Have a seat.

09:06.270 --> 09:13.000
As of the Library's rest day, I will be stepping down from the post of Kanto Library Base Commander.

09:13.000 --> 09:18.040
I would like to give some words of farewell before my departure.

09:18.490 --> 09:25.870
The reason for my resignation is not because of the public's accusations regarding the other day.

09:25.870 --> 09:27.340
As the Library Force Commander,

09:27.340 --> 09:37.200
it was impermissible of me to not have noticed that the Mito Station was disabled, causing tremendous damage to the Library Force.

09:37.200 --> 09:46.040
Freedom of expression is a necessity for all people, and we are all born with it.

09:46.040 --> 09:52.040
There is no need for you to falter in fighting against the force that is taking away that freedom.

09:54.460 --> 09:56.690
Commander Inamine...

09:56.690 --> 09:59.030
The man who built the Library Force.

09:59.750 --> 10:03.990
We have no comments regarding that case.

10:03.990 --> 10:08.190
Then may I have your personal opinion on it?

10:08.190 --> 10:12.630
It's past the Library's business hours, so please allow me to end this conversation.

10:13.590 --> 10:16.850
Man, they're so persistent, day after day!

10:16.850 --> 10:18.770
People from the TV stations?

10:18.770 --> 10:22.980
They're gathered around the gate, so I can't even go out to shop.

10:22.980 --> 10:26.640
They want a victim to fire at.

10:44.830 --> 10:46.670
Yes, that's right.

10:46.670 --> 10:48.210
No doubt about it.

10:48.210 --> 10:53.190
A Library Officer Second Class is hospitalized here, and she's visiting him every day.

10:56.640 --> 11:00.450
"This is outrageous!"

11:00.450 --> 11:04.300
"It is rough to resort to force before deciding the right or wrong of it!"

11:04.300 --> 11:06.130
"Outrageous indeed!"

11:06.130 --> 11:07.890
"Another clout."

11:07.890 --> 11:13.710
"'Nothing but walloping will be effective on you scheming guys.' The remark was followed by a shower of blows."

11:15.730 --> 11:20.650
Outrageous indeed!

11:21.120 --> 11:25.200
This protagonist sounds like you.

11:29.010 --> 11:30.930
You're a member of the Library Force, right?

11:31.710 --> 11:34.350
Um, I...

11:34.350 --> 11:36.800
You're Kasahara from the Task Force, right?

11:37.540 --> 11:38.960
Please stop!

11:38.960 --> 11:40.090
Please!

11:40.090 --> 11:41.840
Please give us a word!

11:42.580 --> 11:43.890
Shibasaki, we've got trouble!

11:43.890 --> 11:45.550
It's Kasahara!

11:46.010 --> 11:47.970
Why, they...

11:47.970 --> 11:50.770
Please give us a comment about the Cleansing Force's casualties.

11:50.770 --> 11:52.870
Please!

11:52.870 --> 11:53.770
Hey!

12:15.560 --> 12:19.670
Train yourself so you'll always be calm under any circumstances, and not overcome by your emotions.

12:20.330 --> 12:22.920
Not overcome by my emotions...

12:25.640 --> 12:29.350
Head-on Interview!
Close-up on Kanto
Library Force, Task Force Member

12:26.350 --> 12:28.240
Let me make this clear.

12:28.240 --> 12:33.310
We also have a legal basis called the Freedom of Library Act.

12:34.370 --> 12:40.780
I heard that my superior officer was greatly impressed when he read this book in his youth.

12:41.440 --> 12:44.030
There are many books that mean a lot to me as well.

12:44.750 --> 12:54.500
Movies, TV shows, music, anime... everything that people have expressed makes my life richer.

12:54.500 --> 12:56.000
Have you ever experienced that?

12:57.000 --> 13:01.050
I believe it is wrong for anyone to have the right to take that freedom away.

13:02.220 --> 13:04.680
But still, a rule is a rule.

13:07.620 --> 13:10.260
Outrageous Indeed

13:11.270 --> 13:16.860
If we follow unjust laws without ever questioning them,

13:16.860 --> 13:19.230
I don't call that living.

13:21.890 --> 13:24.680
The flower impressed here is the chamomile.

13:24.680 --> 13:27.340
It means "Energy in adversity."

13:29.300 --> 13:34.770
The Library Force is currently going through a terrible storm.

13:34.770 --> 13:38.790
But we will never give in!

13:38.790 --> 13:43.060
We will protect what we must protect!

13:48.200 --> 13:52.260
It's a sound argument, but it's only the opinion of the Library Force.

13:53.930 --> 13:55.610
However,

13:55.610 --> 13:58.680
perhaps it's needed in this day and age

13:58.680 --> 14:00.520
to have someone like that.

14:04.320 --> 14:05.990
Excuse us, Miss Kasahara!

14:05.990 --> 14:08.410
Please give us a word!

14:08.410 --> 14:09.400
Hey!

14:09.400 --> 14:10.450
Miss Kasahara!

14:15.820 --> 14:17.160
Well done!

14:17.160 --> 14:19.190
Good job.

14:19.190 --> 14:20.680
I'm sorry.

14:20.680 --> 14:25.820
I broke the request to not give any comments to the media.

14:25.820 --> 14:27.120
Don't worry.

14:27.120 --> 14:30.680
You're the one who said that following rules isn't the only option.

14:30.680 --> 14:34.450
But was it okay to say that on TV?

14:34.450 --> 14:39.020
Judging subjectively, it was our one-sided argument.

14:39.020 --> 14:42.180
I don't think the public opinion will change just from that.

14:42.180 --> 14:43.020
But...

14:43.020 --> 14:46.650
it was great that you said what we all felt!

14:51.570 --> 14:53.590
Disband the Library Force!

14:51.570 --> 14:55.410
Closed

14:53.590 --> 14:55.410
Don't resist censorship!

15:03.120 --> 15:04.710
Commander Inamine.

15:05.160 --> 15:06.800
Thank you.

15:28.190 --> 15:29.680
What's this about?

15:29.680 --> 15:31.970
They're here by their own will.

15:31.970 --> 15:34.280
All of the administrative staff are here as well.

15:34.280 --> 15:36.910
To Kanto Library Base Commander Inamine...

15:36.910 --> 15:38.250
Salute!

15:56.560 --> 16:02.030
Dear, what do you think of what I've done?

16:02.030 --> 16:06.350
I was deeply sinful, after all.

16:06.350 --> 16:10.400
But we also had people who agreed with us.

16:12.150 --> 16:16.130
What's this pile of letters about?!

16:16.130 --> 16:18.060
I brought those in.

16:18.060 --> 16:19.330
Captain Genda!

16:19.330 --> 16:21.600
You shouldn't be moving around!

16:21.600 --> 16:23.320
Don't be so fussy.

16:23.320 --> 16:24.720
Anyway, look.

16:24.720 --> 16:31.560
Letters of encouragement from the people who saw your speech on TV are flooding in.

16:31.560 --> 16:33.180
People who love books,

16:33.660 --> 16:36.180
people who admire art.

16:36.180 --> 16:42.520
Their voices aren't loud, but there are obviously people who side with us.

16:55.820 --> 16:57.770
It's not just the letters.

16:57.770 --> 16:58.710
Look.

17:03.570 --> 17:05.210
Are they...

17:05.650 --> 17:08.330
Are all of them...

17:08.330 --> 17:10.170
Yes, they are.

17:13.510 --> 17:17.680
Captain Genda, may I have some of these?

17:17.680 --> 17:19.390
They were mostly addressed to you.

17:19.390 --> 17:21.630
You can take them all.

17:21.630 --> 17:22.920
Thank you!

17:32.080 --> 17:35.370
Instructor, do you recognize this smell?

17:35.370 --> 17:37.230
It's chamomile.

17:37.230 --> 17:44.410
After I talked about the flower on TV, lots of people who support us sent them in.

17:49.290 --> 17:51.560
We'll get going.

17:51.560 --> 17:52.970
We'll leave the rest with you.

17:52.970 --> 17:55.490
Yeah, thanks.

17:55.490 --> 17:57.360
Is there anything else we can help with?

17:57.360 --> 17:59.380
It's my day off today...

18:00.320 --> 18:01.760
Shibasaki! Stop!

18:06.210 --> 18:09.940
I was shocked when I learned it at first.

18:09.940 --> 18:13.860
You know, that you were my prince.

18:15.560 --> 18:18.860
But it wasn't just then.

18:18.860 --> 18:23.580
You were always my prince.

18:26.000 --> 18:30.920
I've been avoiding the truth,

18:30.920 --> 18:34.170
but I now know it clearly.

18:35.290 --> 18:41.060
Do you remember how we saw these together?

18:43.000 --> 18:46.100
It's not the prince I saw in my high school days,

18:49.700 --> 18:54.900
but <i>you</i> I'm in love with, the man who's right in front of me now.

19:00.640 --> 19:04.440
I said things so boldly on TV,

19:04.440 --> 19:07.130
but without you...

19:07.130 --> 19:08.630
So...

19:08.630 --> 19:10.170
Please...

19:23.430 --> 19:25.720
Why are you crying?

19:32.130 --> 19:35.020
It's nothing.

19:38.450 --> 19:46.950
It's because the thing I value the most just returned to me.

20:18.690 --> 20:21.110
Dear Dad, Mom.

20:21.110 --> 20:23.280
I hope you're doing as well as before.

20:23.940 --> 20:26.330
After that concerning incident,

20:26.330 --> 20:29.610
both Instructor Dojo and Captain Genda have fully recovered.

20:29.610 --> 20:32.210
Everything is back to normal.

20:32.210 --> 20:37.260
The critical outcry of the public against the Library Force has started to calm down,

20:37.260 --> 20:42.240
largely because of the advocacy campaigns led by Orikuchi from Sin Se Sou Publications, despite strict censorship.

20:40.610 --> 20:43.950
nani ka ga kawaru kigashita

20:40.610 --> 20:43.950
I had a feeling something was about to change

20:43.950 --> 20:47.330
nani mo kawaranu asa ni

20:43.950 --> 20:47.330
on this very ordinary morning

20:44.090 --> 20:53.770
Shibasaki told me that Tezuka's older brother worked with the Ministry of Justice to stop the biased TV programming as well.

20:47.330 --> 20:52.340
itsu mo yori sukoshi ii mezamedatta

20:47.330 --> 20:52.340
I woke up feeling a little better than usual

20:53.960 --> 20:57.360
tsurara no you ni sasatta

20:53.960 --> 20:57.360
Someone's laughter that pierced through me

20:54.150 --> 21:00.190
Letters of encouragements and packages of chamomile are still coming in to the base.

20:57.360 --> 21:02.410
dare ka no waraigoe ga tokete

20:57.360 --> 21:02.410
like an icicle, is now melting

21:00.190 --> 21:08.370
I'm still keeping up with my training in order to respond to those people who support us.

21:02.410 --> 21:06.460
haru ga ibuku

21:02.410 --> 21:06.460
as I felt the breath of spring arrive.

21:07.440 --> 21:14.120
hito sashiyubi de sashimesu no wa mirai

21:07.440 --> 21:14.120
My index finger points out to the future

21:14.120 --> 21:23.790
kimi no te no hira ga fureru tabi ni afuru omoi

21:14.120 --> 21:23.790
My thoughts overflow each time
I touch your palm

21:15.170 --> 21:17.710
Kasahara! Keep your arms up!

21:18.260 --> 21:19.380
Yes, Sir!

21:24.240 --> 21:27.770
ch-ch-ch-changes saa kawatteku

21:24.240 --> 21:27.770
Changes, yeah. I'm changing.

21:27.770 --> 21:31.090
sayonara furui jibun

21:27.770 --> 21:31.090
Goodbye my old self

21:31.090 --> 21:37.620
shingenjitsu atarashii nani ka ga matteru

21:31.090 --> 21:37.620
There's something new awaiting me in the new reality

21:37.620 --> 21:41.360
ch-ch-ch-changes saa kawatteku

21:37.620 --> 21:41.360
Changes, yeah. I'm changing.

21:41.360 --> 21:44.590
ushinau mono mo aru

21:41.360 --> 21:44.590
There are things I'll lose too

21:44.590 --> 21:50.360
demo iindesu hitotsu unazuki kakedasu

21:44.590 --> 21:50.360
But that's okay, I'll just nod and keep running

21:50.360 --> 21:57.910
saa subete ga ima kawatteku subete ga hajimaru

21:50.360 --> 21:57.910
Yeah, everything is changing now, everything starts now

21:57.910 --> 22:08.200
shingenjitsu dare no mono demo nai atarashii jibun

21:57.910 --> 22:08.200
It's a new reality, my new self belongs to no one but me
